invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_verify.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p384_wide_verify
reason: the host verifier multiplies a hash it did not reduce modulo
  n. The Montgomery product happens to take any left operand, so every
  verdict stays right, and a hash of n or more is one hash in 2^190.
  p384_wide_field.h takes operands below the modulus, and the proof
  requires that of every scalar the verifier hands a product.

--- old
    if (p384_wide_compare(e, p384_wide_modn.m) >= 0) {
        (void)p384_wide_sub_raw(e, e, p384_wide_modn.m);
    }
--- new
